        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{19}{73}$",
          "html": "<div class=\"option-content question\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --> $\\frac{19}{73}$ <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": "C",
      "explanation_text": "The given expression is $\\frac{x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1}{x^{4}+4x^{3}+6x^{2}+4x+1}$ We can recognize both numerator and denominator using identities. $x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1=(x+1)^{3}$ and $x^{4}+4x^{3}+6x^{2}+4x+1=(x+1)^{4}$ So the expression becomes $\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{(x+1)^{4}}$ Cancel the common factor $(x+1)^{3}$ : $\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{(x+1)^{4}}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ Now put $x=2$ : $\\frac{1}{2+1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ So the correct option is $\\frac{1}{3}$ Option C.",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>The given expression is</p>\n<p> $\\frac{x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1}{x^{4}+4x^{3}+6x^{2}+4x+1}$ </p>\n<p>We can recognize both numerator and denominator using identities.</p>\n<p> $x^{3}+3x^{2}+3x+1=(x+1)^{3}$ </p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p> $x^{4}+4x^{3}+6x^{2}+4x+1=(x+1)^{4}$ </p>\n<p>So the expression becomes</p>\n<p> $\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{(x+1)^{4}}$ </p>\n<p>Cancel the common factor  $(x+1)^{3}$ :</p>\n<p> $\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{(x+1)^{4}}=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ </p>\n<p>Now put  $x=2$ :</p>\n<p> $\\frac{1}{2+1}=\\frac{1}{3}$ </p>\n<p>So the correct option is</p>\n<p> $\\frac{1}{3}$ </p>\n<p>Option C.</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
      "has_image": false,
