      "explanation_text": "A binomial expansion $(ax+b)^{k}$ has $k+1$ distinct terms. Here $k=3n$ , so: Number of terms $=3n+1$ . Set $3n+1=22$ : $3n+1=22$ $3n=21$ $n=7$ Answer: 7 (Option C).",
      "explanation_html": "<div class=\"question q-prose\"><!-- HTML_TAG_START --><p>A binomial expansion  $(ax+b)^{k}$  has  $k+1$  distinct terms. Here  $k=3n$ , so:</p>\n<p><p>Number of terms  $=3n+1$ .  </p></p>\n<p><p>Set  $3n+1=22$ :  </p>\n<p> $3n+1=22$  </p>\n<p> $3n=21$  </p>\n<p> $n=7$  </p></p>\n<p>Answer: 7 (Option C).</p><!-- HTML_TAG_END --></div>",
