      "explanation_text": "The total number of terms in the expansion of $(x+a)^{n}-(x-a)^{n}$ is determined based on whether the exponent $n$ is odd or even. If $n$ is odd: $\\text{Total number of terms}=\\frac{n+1}{2}$ If $n$ is even: $\\text{Total number of terms}=\\frac{n}{2}$ In this specific case, we're looking at the expansion of $(x+a)^{47}-(x-a)^{47}$ . Since 47 is an odd number: $\\text{Total number of terms}=\\frac{47+1}{2}=\\frac{48}{2}=24$",
